issues.what:
The S0b act is specified only for a text-only stream and is wrong once media is interleaved (S4 onward). The S0b LOOP row computes b0 = byte_pos[k0]. For a media position, byte_pos is the clip's anchor, so re-tokenizing from b0 and re-interleaving would re-emit a partly consumed clip. 0b.3 says the splice goes 'after the unit under the cursor' (D1's record rule), which contradicts the S0b row. Also unresolved:
- TOK.interleave on the tail;
- who builds the spliced Segmentation (TOK's record type; bytes_per_token of a spliced record);
- TOK.tokenize's cache counts a new-start call as tok.segment, not tok.retok.
The 'bpe' arm cannot be combined with 'codes cut just in time' (L2): merges are applied to codes as they were at act time, and re-encoding at cut changes lengths inside a laid-out window.
